# jemdoc: nofooter
==Qinghua Liu

~~~
{}{img_left}{photo-24 copy.JPG}{alt text}{228}{254}


I'm a researcher in (mid, post]-training at [https://openai.com/ OpenAI].

I'm privileged to be part of an amazing team working on the critical path to shipping Codex and ChatGPT, including [https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-5-5/ GPT-5.5], [https://openai.com/index/gpt-5-6/ GPT-5.6], and the next generation of models. I also very indirectly contributed to specialized models such as [https://openai.com/index/gpt-5-5-with-trusted-access-for-cyber/ GPT‑5.5‑Cyber]  and [https://openai.com/index/introducing-new-capabilities-to-gpt-rosalind/ GPT‑Rosalind]. Earlier, I worked on model personalities, which was integrated into [https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-5/ GPT-5] and [https://openai.com/index/gpt-5-1/ GPT-5.1]. 




I received Ph.D. from Princeton, advised by [https://sites.google.com/view/cjin/home Chi Jin]. 
My PhD works focused on RL theory, including partially observable RL ([https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.08967 POMDP], 
[https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.14997 PSR], [PORL_Survey.pdf Survey]), multi-agent RL ([https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.14555 Stochastic Game]), 
 and   RL with large state spaces ([https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.00815 Function Approximation]). During PhD, I've interned at DeepMind London with [https://sites.ualberta.ca/~szepesva/ Csaba Szepesvári]. After PhD, I spent a wonderful year as a postdoctoral researcher at [https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/theme/machine-learning-ai-nyc/people/ Microsoft Research NYC].



Even earlier, I received a  B.E. in Electrical Engineering and a B.S. in Mathematics from Tsinghua University.




#I will be joining WashU CS as an assistant professor in the fall of 2025.

[https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=CotFJJsAAAAJ&hl=en Google Scholar], [https://x.com/Qinghua_Liu_ Twitter]


 ~~~



